WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.616 --> 00:00:17.858
the next morning, Katie ran up the hill to the pond.

2
00:00:19.039 --> 00:00:22.261
Dad and Joy were already working on the tree house steps.

3
00:00:22.281 --> 00:00:27.504
"Morning, Dad," called Katie, climbing into the back of the truck.

4
00:00:28.624 --> 00:00:31.546
She looked in the old bucket and pulled out the pulley.

5
00:00:31.566 --> 00:00:32.647
"What's this?"

6
00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:36.510
"It's a pulley of course," said Joy.

7
00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:38.752
"What's it for?"

8
00:00:39.252 --> 00:00:39.892
asked Katie.

9
00:00:39.912 --> 00:00:42.975
"You'll see," Joy answered.

10
00:00:42.995 --> 00:00:45.997
"Hey," said Katie.

11
00:00:46.017 --> 00:00:48.759
"I can use this pole for my wind sock."

12
00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.161
"What's a wind sock?"

13
00:00:51.641 --> 00:00:52.262
asked Joy.

14
00:00:52.282 --> 00:00:55.324
"You'll see," answered Katie.

15
00:00:57.176 --> 00:00:59.678
Pieces of the tin roof were spread on the grass.

16
00:01:00.939 --> 00:01:03.161
Dad opened a can of dark blue paint.

17
00:01:04.262 --> 00:01:06.304
"Here's a brush," he said to Joy.

18
00:01:06.324 --> 00:01:07.765
"Do you want to help, Katie?"

19
00:01:09.026 --> 00:01:12.349
"Nope," Katie said and jumped down from the truck.

20
00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.252
"Mom and I are working on something.

21
00:01:15.652 --> 00:01:16.273
See you later."

22
00:01:19.836 --> 00:01:24.460
Joy dipped her brush into the paint and carefully painted the first piece of tin.

23
00:01:30.444 --> 00:01:36.129
"This roof has to look perfect," Joy said to herself as she turned to dip her brush again.

24
00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:41.454
When she turned back, Magoo was sitting on the freshly painted tin.

25
00:01:41.474 --> 00:01:44.316
"Magoo!" she said.

26
00:01:44.336 --> 00:01:45.978
"It's wet paint!"

27
00:01:47.259 --> 00:01:52.163
Magoo got up and licked Joy's face, his blue tail wagging happily.

28
00:01:52.183 --> 00:01:55.366
"Get out of here," cried Joy.

29
00:01:55.386 --> 00:01:57.148
"You'll spill the paint."

30
00:01:58.308 --> 00:02:00.590
Magoo leaped back and sat down again.

31
00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:03.633
"Good boy," said Joy.

32
00:02:04.914 --> 00:02:06.435
Magoo watched Joy paint.

33
00:02:07.016 --> 00:02:10.219
His eyes were fixed on the brush as it moved back and forth.

34
00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.742
Then he reached out and touched the brush with his paw.

35
00:02:15.883 --> 00:02:17.785
"Stop!" cried Joy.

36
00:02:17.805 --> 00:02:19.987
"Do you want to be a blue Magoo?"

37
00:02:21.208 --> 00:02:25.452
The dog pulled back his blue paw and gave Joy a sorry look.

38
00:02:27.104 --> 00:02:32.967
By noon the steps were finished, the tin pieces were painted, and Dad was building the walls.

39
00:02:34.228 --> 00:02:36.529
Joy and Magoo were lying in the grass.

40
00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:46.294
They were both covered with paint: her shirt, his paws, her knees, his tail, her chin, his ear.

41
00:02:47.455 --> 00:02:48.575
But Joy didn't care.

42
00:02:49.056 --> 00:02:51.097
The tree house would be finished soon!

43
00:02:52.257 --> 00:02:55.679
The next afternoon, Dad put in the door and the window.

44
00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.496
Finally he nailed down the roof.

45
00:02:58.516 --> 00:03:00.537
"It's done!"

46
00:03:01.237 --> 00:03:02.037
shouted Joy.

47
00:03:02.597 --> 00:03:05.738
Katie, Mom, and Grandpa ran from the house to see.

48
00:03:06.959 --> 00:03:09.359
Mom brought a flowerpot filled with daisies.

49
00:03:09.379 --> 00:03:12.120
"Put it in the bucket, Mom!"

50
00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.201
Joy shouted from the tree house.

51
00:03:15.421 --> 00:03:19.022
The bucket was sitting on the ground with a rope tied to its handle.

52
00:03:20.202 --> 00:03:23.783
The rope was attached to the pulley, which was attached to the roof.

53
00:03:25.123 --> 00:03:27.044
Mom set the flowers in the bucket.

54
00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:30.701
"Now watch this," called Joy.

55
00:03:31.881 --> 00:03:35.982
She pulled on the rope, the pulley turned, and the bucket rose.

56
00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:39.443
Joy lifted the daisies out of the bucket.

57
00:03:39.823 --> 00:03:40.904
"Come on up, Mom!"

58
00:03:42.244 --> 00:03:47.686
One by one everyone took a turn looking out on the Donovans' land from the tree house.

59
00:03:49.306 --> 00:03:51.887
Everyone opened and shut the tree house door.

60
00:03:53.087 --> 00:03:56.088
They looked out the window and tried out the pulley.

61
00:03:58.496 --> 00:04:01.359
"Let's give a big cheer for Dad and Joy!"

62
00:04:01.999 --> 00:04:02.840
shouted Katie.

63
00:04:04.381 --> 00:04:07.384
Mom, Grandpa, and Katie clapped and cheered.

64
00:04:08.184 --> 00:04:09.065
Dad bowed.

65
00:04:09.586 --> 00:04:10.706
Joy beamed.

66
00:04:10.726 --> 00:04:14.009
"One more thing," said Katie.

67
00:04:14.029 --> 00:04:17.432
"Dad put up the new wind sock on the tree house roof.

68
00:04:18.653 --> 00:04:21.375
Look! You can see it hanging from the pole."

69
00:04:22.657 --> 00:04:24.598
Everyone looked up at the wind sock.

70
00:04:25.139 --> 00:04:26.520
"Mom helped me make it."

71
00:04:27.832 --> 00:04:29.814
"Wow!" said Joy.

72
00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:36.759
"A wind sock tells us the strength and direction of the wind," explained Katie.

73
00:04:36.779 --> 00:04:40.903
"When the wind is still, the wind sock just hangs."

74
00:04:40.923 --> 00:04:44.746
"Like it's doing right now," said Grandpa.

75
00:04:44.766 --> 00:04:47.888
"That's right," Katie said.

76
00:04:47.908 --> 00:04:52.812
"But when the wind is strong, the wind sock flies straight out!"

77
00:04:53.973 --> 00:04:56.916
Katie paused and opened her eyes extra wide.

78
00:04:58.112 --> 00:05:02.098
"And if that wind is coming from the southwest, look out!

79
00:05:02.618 --> 00:05:04.581
It might be tornado time!"

80
00:05:04.601 --> 00:05:08.126
"That's pretty cool, Katie," said Joy.

81
00:05:08.146 --> 00:05:09.167
"Thanks!"
